# Review routing for the files where a wrong merge is not a bug but a
# loophole. Everything else in this repo is reviewable by anyone; these are
# the paths whose whole purpose is to constrain what agents may do, so a
# change to them cannot be self-approved by the change that needs it.
#
# CODEOWNERS is advisory until branch protection requires owner review. It is
# checked in first so the requirement has something to point at.

# Default: everything has an owner, so nothing lands unlooked-at.
*                               @juzser

# The severity ladder, budget caps, crosscheck quorum. Editing these changes
# what stops the line and what merges — for every epic, retroactively.
/factory/policies/               @juzser

# The mechanical half of the safety model (README § Safety model): the hook
# that blocks pushes to main and the settings that decide which tools an
# agent may call at all. guardrails.md is the prose; this is the enforcement.
/.claude/hooks/                  @juzser
/.claude/settings.json           @juzser

# Spec contracts are the dispatch precondition — "no contract, no dispatch".
# A loosened schema is a task spec that no longer has to say what it claims.
/factory/specs/schema/           @juzser

# The gate itself, and the workflow that runs it. If check.sh can be edited
# as freely as the code it checks, it is not a gate.
/scripts/check.sh                @juzser
/.github/workflows/              @juzser
/.gitleaks.toml                  @juzser
